# API Endpoints and Their Purposes

## 1. Health Check API

**Base category:** Health Endpoints  
**Authentication:** Not required

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/health` | Checks overall system health, including database connectivity, workers, and queue status. |
| GET | `/health/live` | Checks whether the application process is running. |
| GET | `/health/ready` | Checks whether PostgreSQL is reachable and background workers are running. |

## 2. Authentication API

**Base path:** `/api/auth/`

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/api/auth/v1/login/` | Authenticates a user using OAuth2 form data, with email as the username. |
| POST | `/api/auth/login-json` | Authenticates a user using a JSON request body. |
| POST | `/api/auth/refresh` | Refreshes an access token using a refresh token. |
| POST | `/api/auth/logout` | Logs out the user by deleting the token on the client side. |
| POST | `/api/auth/verify-token` | Verifies whether the current access token is valid. |
| POST | `/api/auth/change-password` | Changes the password of the authenticated user. |
| POST | `/api/auth/request-password-reset` | Requests a password reset and sends a reset email. |
| POST | `/api/auth/reset-password` | Resets a password using a token received by email. |

## 3. User Management API

**Base path:** `/api/user/`

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/api/user/v1/signup/` | Creates a new user; requires the `create_user` permission. |
| POST | `/api/user/v1/login/` | Authenticates a user using email and password, with rate limiting. |
| POST | `/api/user/v1/token/` | Provides OAuth2 password-flow authentication for the Swagger Authorize interface. |
| POST | `/api/user/v1/refresh/` | Exchanges a refresh token for a new access-token and refresh-token pair. |
| POST | `/api/user/v1/logout/` | Revokes the current access token. |
| POST | `/api/user/v1/change-password/` | Changes the authenticated user's password and invalidates previous tokens. |
| GET | `/api/user/v1/me/` | Returns the current user's profile, role, and permissions. |
| GET | `/api/user/v1/all/users/` | Lists users with pagination and filtering options. |
| GET | `/api/user/{id}` | Retrieves a specific user; accessible to the user themselves or users with `read_user` permission. |
| PATCH | `/api/user/{id}` | Updates user information, including username, email, password, role, and account status. |
| DELETE | `/api/user/{id}` | Soft-deletes a user. Permanent deletion is restricted to superusers. |
| POST | `/api/user/{id}/restore` | Restores a soft-deleted user. |
| POST | `/api/user/{id}/permissions/{permission_id}` | Grants a permission directly to a user. |
| DELETE | `/api/user/{id}/permissions/{permission_id}` | Revokes a permission directly from a user. |

## 4. Role Management API

