## 14. Key System Features

### Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
Provides role- and permission-based access control for protected operations, allowing access to be managed at the user and role levels.

### Soft Deletion and Restoration
Supports soft deletion for many entities, allowing records to be restored instead of permanently removed. Permanent deletion is restricted to superusers where implemented.

### Audit Trail
Records sensitive actions to support accountability, monitoring, and troubleshooting.

### Asynchronous Event Processing
Accepts events through ingestion endpoints and processes them through a queue-based background workflow.

### Analytics and Monitoring
Provides event statistics, failure rates, processing latency, source analysis, queue status, and dead-letter monitoring.

### Rate Limiting
Applies request limits to protect selected API endpoints against excessive requests and abuse.

### Idempotency
Supports idempotency keys for event ingestion to help prevent duplicate processing when requests are retried.

### Real-Time Notifications
Uses Server-Sent Events (SSE) to deliver live event-processing updates to connected clients.

### API Key Authentication
Allows API keys to authenticate event-ingestion requests and supports key creation, listing, updating, revocation, and deletion.

